6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a fixed,
durable written document that provides the Corresponding Source on a
durable physical medium customarily used for software interchange.

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a written
offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as long as you
offer spare parts or customer service for that product, to give
anyone who possesses the object code either a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium customarily used
for software interchange, or access to a copy from a network server
at no charge, by a standard interface (such as HTTP).

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium customarily used for
software interchange, if you do not convey the object code more than
occasionally.

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated place
(gratis or for a charge), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
further charge. You need not require the recipients to copy the
Corresponding Source along with the object code. If the place to
copy the object code is a network server, the Corresponding Source
may be on a different server (operated by you or a third party)
that supports equivalent access for all the recipients, and you must
maintain the Corresponding Source so long as you maintain the object
code.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer transmission, provided
you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source and object code
are being offered to the public at no charge under this License. This
provision is not intended to include, and does not require,
conveying any personal or private communications.

A separable portion of the object code, whose source code is excluded
from the Corresponding Source as a System Library, need not be
included in the Corresponding Source.

