11. Patents.

A "contributor" is a copyright holder who authorizes the use under
this License of the claims of a patent that the contributor can
license. The "essential claims" of a patent are those claims that
would, in some way, intrude into the space occupied by the Program and
its covered work. A "contributing patent" is a patent that has at
least one essential claim by a contributor.

Each contributor grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free
patent license under the contributor's essential claims to make, use,
sell, offer for sale, import and otherwise run, modify and propagate
the content of its contributing patent in any covered work. If you
convey a covered work, you must, under the patent license provisions
of this License, give reasonable notice to the downstream recipients
of the covered work about the patent licenses. If you convey a covered
work and the conveyance does not contain an offer to provide the
Corresponding Source, the patent license will be invalid.

If you, or a party you are bound to, institute patent litigation
against any entity (including a cross-claim or counterclaim in a
lawsuit) alleging that a covered work infringes a patent, then your
patent license from the contributor terminates under this License.

If, pursuant to or in connection with a single transaction or
arrangement, you convey, or are bound to convey, a covered work, and
the litigation has not been terminated by a court order or other
agreement, the patent license from each contributor terminates
automatically under this License.

